## Immutable indexed polygon topology, shared by procedural geometry consumers.
## Operators return new meshes; input snapshots never change. No editor state.
##
## Storage is structure-of-arrays: f32 positions relative to an f64 origin,
## i32 face offsets and corner points, f32 face normals and i32 display
## triangles, each a shared column. What connectivity alone determines (the
## face of each corner, edges, point-face incidence, the connectivity hash) is
## a lazy cache shared by every mesh with the same topology; the spatial index
## is lazy per geometry and refits after a Move. Construction validates and
## computes normals and triangles in parallel.
##
## A precise mesh also keeps its f64 points. B-rep tessellation builds its
## chart meshes this way, since trims resolve features far below f32 spacing;
## `point`, normals, triangulation and derived meshes then use the f64 points,
## while display and spatial queries use the f32 positions as always.
